# The build context is the repository root, so this keeps a gigabyte of things
# the image does not want out of the upload. Named for the Dockerfile beside it,
# which is how BuildKit scopes an ignore file to one build.
.venv/
venv/
*-venv/

.git/
.claude/

# **The files that hold each developer's own values.** All of them are
# gitignored, so none is usually here — but a build context is not the place to
# find out.
#
# **`**` matters here.** A bare `.env` matches the context root only, and `COPY .`
# reaches every directory's own file. Naming each one by path instead is a list
# that goes stale on the commit that moves one.
**/.env
**/.env.*
# Except the examples, which hold no secret by rule.
!**/.env.example
environments.yaml

# `**` matters here too. Without it these match only at the context root, and a
# stale `tests/__pycache__` goes into the image, where a traceback then points at
# the host's own file paths and prints `???` for source it cannot read.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
node_modules/
